# CONTROL: §12 TAIL guarantees proper tail calls. Ten million tail frames
# complete with the right answer and no signal. The NON-tail half of the row
# is measured separately, in `depth.id`, because it does not survive.
# expect: 10000000
# @corpus current
tail: i64 = (n: i64, acc: i64)
  if n <= 0
    acc
  tail(n - 1, acc + 1)

a = tail(10000000, 0)
print("{a}")
# The explicit `0` tail, for the reason bytes.id and invalid.id carry theirs:
# `print` is void-shaped, so `blockTailResult` walks back to the last
# value-carrying binding and the MODULE's result became `a`. 10000000 & 0xFF
# is 128, so this file printed exactly what its oracle demanded and still
# contradicted it on the exit status. Same defect nul.id carried.
0
